  {
    "abstract": "This paper examines the importance of US trade policy uncertainty in determining downside risk in stock markets across the US and other major economies. The findings indicate that heightened US trade policy uncertainty significantly increases the downside risk to future stock returns, both domestically and globally. The effect of trade policy uncertainty persists over several months and is more pronounced in the lower tail than at the median of the return distribution. Notably, elevated trade policy uncertainty accounts for about 30 percent of the variation in predicted S&P 500 returns during early 2025.",
